    "cost_closing_html":  "About \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}} a bowl\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost) for pad kee mao that would run $14 at a Thai restaurant. Fourteen bowls here costs less than three there, and yours has more pork in it.",
    "shop_smart":  [
                       "Ground pork covers the protein at about 3.75 pounds. It is consistently cheaper than the sliced pork most stir fry recipes call for, and it browns faster too.",
                       "Rice noodles are the other big line. Buy them from the international aisle or an Asian market and that number can drop by a third.",
                       "Fish sauce, soy sauce, and rice vinegar are all buy-once bottles that live in the pantry. This batch uses just a splash of soy and vinegar off bottles that season months of cooking."
                   ],
    "make_it":  [
                    "Weigh your empty mixing pot and write the number down for portioning later.",
                    "Soak or boil the rice noodles per the package until just shy of tender, then drain and rinse. They finish in the pan.",
                    "Stir together the fish sauce, soy sauce, and rice vinegar for the sauce.",
                    "Heat the vegetable oil in your largest skillet or pot over high heat. Cook the onion 2 minutes, then add the garlic and jalapeno for 1 minute more.",
                    "Add the ground pork and brown it hard, breaking it into crumbles, until cooked through with crispy edges. Season with the salt and black pepper as it browns.",
                    "Add the noodles and the sauce and toss until the noodles soak it up and everything is coated.",
                    "Kill the heat and fold in the fresh basil, sliced bell pepper, and lime juice. The basil should wilt in the residual heat, not cook."
                ],
